  "question": {
    "text": "If the integral $\\int \\frac{5 \\tan x}{\\tan x-2} d x=x+a \\ln |\\sin x-2 \\cos x|+k$, then $a$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gFiN4",
      "text": "\n$-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9SjzJ",
      "text": "\n$-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ixWFa",
      "text": "\n$1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zIl2O",
      "text": "\n$2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int \\frac{5 \\tan x}{\\tan x-2} d x=\\int \\frac{5 \\sin x}{\\sin x-2 \\cos x} d x$\n$\\Rightarrow \\int\\left[\\frac{2(\\cos x+2 \\sin x)+(\\sin x-2 \\cos x)}{\\sin x-2 \\cos x}\\right] d x$\n$=2 \\int\\left(\\frac{\\cos x+2 \\sin x}{\\sin x-2 \\cos x}\\right) d x+\\int d x+k$\n$=2 \\log |\\sin x-2 \\cos x|+x+k \\quad \\therefore a=2$",
    "image": null
  },
